## Key design decisions

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Bulk-safe** | Single loop over `getSobjs()`; no SOQL; O(n) per trigger invocation |
| **Field-level error** | `error(msg, opp, Opportunity.Amount)` calls `opp.addError(msg)` internally — only the offending record is blocked, others in the batch save normally |
| **Testability** | The `error()` helper also populates `fflib_SObjectDomain.getErrors()` so unit tests can assert on the exact message without needing to query the SObject |
| **"Closing as won + changing amount is allowed"** | We check `prev.StageName` (the value *before* this update), not `opp.StageName`. If the previous stage wasn't `Closed Won`, the amount-change rule is simply not applied, even if the new stage *is* `Closed Won` |
| **Null safety on amount comparison** | Apex `!=` on `Decimal` correctly returns `false` when both sides are `null`, and `true` when only one side is `null` — exactly the semantics we want |
| **Trigger** | All events are listed; the fflib trigger handler internally routes to `validateInsert`/`validateUpdate` (before) or commit hooks (after), so the after-context events are a safe no-op for these validation rules |

