public class AccountOnboardingService {

    public static List<Account> createAccountsWithContacts(
        Map<String, List<String>> contactLastNamesByAccountName
    ) {
        if (contactLastNamesByAccountName == null || contactLastNamesByAccountName.isEmpty()) {
            return new List<Account>();
        }

        fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork uow = new fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork();
        List<Account> accounts = new List<Account>();
        List<Contact> contacts = new List<Contact>();

        for (String accountName : contactLastNamesByAccountName.keySet()) {
            Account acc = new Account(Name = accountName);
            uow.markSObject(acc);
            accounts.add(acc);

            List<String> lastNames = contactLastNamesByAccountName.get(accountName);
            if (lastNames != null) {
                for (String lastName : lastNames) {
                    contacts.add(new Contact(LastName = lastName, AccountId = acc.Id));
                }
            }
        }

        if (!contacts.isEmpty()) {
            uow.markSObjects(contacts);
        }

        uow.commitWork();

        return accounts;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

- **Parent-child via sourceId:** After `uow.markSObject(acc)`, fflib assigns a generated sourceId to `acc.Id`. Setting `AccountId = acc.Id` on the Contact lets the UoW resolve the reference to the real Id at commit time — no premature DML needed.
- **Single commit:** All Accounts and Contacts accumulate in one `fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork`; a single `commitWork()` issues one `INSERT` per SObject type, keeping governor limits well within bounds even for hundreds of contacts.
- **Null/empty guard:** Returns an empty list immediately without constructing a UoW or performing any work.
- **Bulk-safe:** The loop over map entries and inner lists is purely in-memory construction; DML is deferred and batched by fflib at commit time.

