```apex
public without sharing class AccountRatingService implements Queueable {

    private final List<Id> accountIds;

    public AccountRatingService(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        this.accountIds = accountIds == null ? new List<Id>() : accountIds.asList();
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext ctx) {
        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Identify which accounts have at least one open opp ≥ 100 000
        Map<Id, Boolean> hasLargeOpenOpp = new Map<Id, Boolean>();
        Set<Id> accountsWithOpenOpps = new Set<Id>();

        for (Opportunity opp : [
            SELECT AccountId, Amount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
              AND IsClosed = false
        ]) {
            accountsWithOpenOpps.add(opp.AccountId);
            if (opp.Amount != null && opp.Amount >= 100_000) {
                hasLargeOpenOpp.put(opp.AccountId, true);
            }
        }

        // Determine the target rating for every account in scope
        Map<Id, String> targetRatings = new Map<Id, String>();
        for (Id accId : accountIds) {
            if (hasLargeOpenOpp.get(accId) == true) {
                targetRatings.put(accId, 'Hot');
            }
            else if (accountsWithOpenOpps.contains(accId)) {
                targetRatings.put(accId, 'Warm');
            }
            else {
                targetRatings.put(accId, 'Cold');
            }
        }

        // Fetch current ratings so we only write what actually changed
        List<Account> current = [
            SELECT Id, Rating
            FROM Account
            WHERE Id IN :accountIds
        ];

        List<Account> toUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Account acc : current) {
            String target = targetRatings.get(acc.Id);
            if (target != null && acc.Rating != target) {
                toUpdate.add(new Account(Id = acc.Id, Rating = target));
            }
        }

        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

### Notes

- **`IsClosed = false`** is the standard way to identify open opportunities. It's driven by the stage's `IsClosed` attribute, so it automatically adapts if you add custom closed stages—no hardcoded stage list to maintain.
- **`without sharing`** on the service class: Queueable jobs run in a system context where the enqueuing user's sharing may not apply uniformly across 200 accounts. If your org has strict sharing and you need to respect it, change to `with sharing` and ensure the automation runs under a user with appropriate access.
- **No DML in the trigger** and **no SOQL in the trigger** keeps the synchronous portion to a single `System.enqueueJob` call—minimal overhead on the opportunity save.
- If you ever need to re-rate all accounts (e.g., after a bulk data load or stage reclassification), you can call `System.enqueueJob(new AccountRatingService(allAccountIds))` from a batch or Apex job.

## What I'd change and why

The suggested approach of calling `PricingRules.standardDiscountFor(line.Product2Id)` once per line in a loop would execute **one SOQL query per call**. With 200 lines per CPQ quote, that's 200 queries — exceeding the 100-query governor limit and causing a `System.LimitExceededException` in production.

The fix: bulk-query `Product2` for all unique `Product2Id` values in a **single** SOQL, then call `PricingRules.standardDiscountForFamily(family)` (which is pure in-memory logic, no SOQL). This keeps the discount rules in `PricingRules` as required, avoids copying them, and stays within governor limits.

